      "output": {
        "message": "A good immediate move is to acknowledge the message without automatically staying late to do it. You can reply with a quick, neutral confirmation that sets the timeline: > \"Got it. I'm heading out for the day, so I'll put this at the top of my list first thing tomorrow morning.\" If you aren't sure whether the supervisor expects it done that evening, you can ask a direct question instead: > \"Received. I'm just about to log off—is this needed tonight, or should I tackle it first thing tomorrow?\" Either way, you confirm you received the task while making your end-of-day boundary clear.",
